"Ali got four $10 notes and six $20 notes after helping Mr. James at his farm. Ali pass his sister half the money he got, then use 3/5 of what left to buy dinner. Calculate how much money he still got after buying the dinner.",Ali has four $10 bills and six $20 bills that he saved after working for Mr. James on his farm. Ali gives her sister half of the total money he has and uses 3/5 of the remaining amount of money to buy dinner. Calculate the amount of money he has after buying the dinner.,32,32,32,32,"Let me solve this step by step.

1. Calculate total money Ali got
* Four $10 notes = 4 × $10 = $40
* Six $20 notes = 6 × $20 = $120
* Total money = $40 + $120 = $160

2. Calculate money after giving half to his sister
* Half of $160 = $160 ÷ 2 = $80
* Money left with Ali = $80

3. Calculate money spent on dinner (3/5 of $80)
* 3/5 × $80 = $48
* Money spent on dinner = $48

4. Calculate remaining money after dinner
* Remaining money = $80 - $48 = $32

